       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose, and the reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for that dose. In a 70 kg patient with normal kidney and liver function, I'd expect it to cause severe hypotension and possibly prolonged shock. Amlodipine's half-life of 30\u201350 hours would make that hard to reverse.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum labeled dose, if you want the strongest standard regimen.\n- **Enter 5 mg once daily** with a plan to titrate up in 1\u20132 weeks.\n- **Add a second agent** if one drug isn't enough. I can enter that order with the dose you choose.\n- **Route the request through pharmacy.** If there's a real clinical reason for a dose this far outside the labeled range, a pharmacist review or a direct order through your usual override process would be the right path. I can add a note to flag it.\n\nIf you want any of these, tell me which and I'll enter it now."
      }
